7)Armstrong number :
Input: n = 153
Output: true
Explanation: Number of digits : 3.
1 + 125 + 27 = 153.
Therefore, it is an Armstrong number.
class Solution {
    public boolean isArmstrong(int n) {
      if(n==0){return true;}
      int count=0;
      int xerox1=n;
      int xerox2=n;
      int sum=0;
      while(xerox1>0){
        xerox1=xerox1/10;
        count++;
      }
      while(xerox2>0){
        int digit = xerox2%10;
        xerox2=xerox2/10;
        sum=sum+(int)Math.pow(digit,count);
      }
      if(n==sum){
        return true;
      }
      return false;
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(d) or equivalently O(log n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
