Input: n = 99
Output: true
Explanation:
Since 99 is divisible by the sum (9 + 9 = 18) plus product (9 * 9 = 81) of its digits (total 99), the output is true.

Example 2:
Input: n = 23
Output: false
Explanation:
Since 23 is not divisible by the sum (2 + 3 = 5) plus product (2 * 3 = 6) of its digits (total 11), the output is fals

class Solution {
    public boolean checkDivisibility(int n) {
       int ns = n;
       int np = n;
       int sum = 0;
       int product = 1;
       while(ns>0){
        sum = sum + (ns%10);
        ns = ns/10;
       }
       while(np>0){
        product=product*(np%10);
        np = np/10;
       }
       if(n%(sum+product)==0){
        return true;
       } 
       else{
        return false;
       }
    }
}
